n class=\"doe-chip\">Excel</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/EPS%20Special%20Education%20Allocation.xlsx\">Summary of Previous Calculations, EPS Special Ed Allocation, and High Cost Out-of-District Adjustment by SAU</a>&nbsp;<span class=\"doe-chip\">Excel</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\" id=\"transportation-eps-operating-allocation-for-2022\"><h2>Transportation EPS Operating Allocation for 2022-23</h2></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/FY23_TranspAlloc_18Jan2022_Webversion.xls\">FY 23&nbsp;EPS Transportation Operating Allocations by SAU</a>&nbsp;<span class=\"doe-chip\">Excel</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"contact\" class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3>Contact</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Charlotte Ellis</strong><br />\r\n<em>School Finance and Compliance Helpdesk Analyst</em><br />\r\n<strong>Phone</strong>: 207-624-6625<br />\r\n<strong>Email</strong>: <a href=\"mailto:charlotte.ellis@maine.gov\">Charlotte.Ellis@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<p class=\"doe-jump\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-top\"><a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a></p>","notes":["503 words with no section headers at all — the biggest single improvement available here."],"decisions":[{"id":"outline","on":true,"label":"Rebuild the heading outline","why":"5 headings sit at a level the page never opens — \"General\" is an h5 with no h4 above it, so it is neither announced nor styled as the sub-section it is. Each heading moves to one level below whatever encloses it.","value":"h5 → h2"},{"id":"blockhead","on":true,"label":"Turn the headings into section headers","why":"5 headings are plain text where every other page uses a section header, so the page reads as one continuous wall instead of parts.","value":"5 sections"},{"id":"emailcase","on":true,"label":"Write the email addresses the same way","why":"1 address is shown in whatever case it was typed in. The house form capitalises each name and leaves a middle initial in lower case — charlotte.ellis@maine.gov → Charlotte.Ellis@maine.gov. Only the first letter of each part changes, so a name that spells itself LaBreck keeps doing so.","value":"1 address"},{"id":"filechip","on":true,"label":"Tag a document link with the format it opens","why":"4 links on this page open a file — 4 Excel — and say nothing about it, while others in the same list carry a tag because their author typed one. The format is read from the file name, so the list stops being half-labelled. No link text changes.","value":"4 links"},{"id":"itemdash","on":true,"label":"Drop the dash once the link is set apart","why":"33 of those items separate the link from its description with a dash. The link is now set in the display face at a larger size with a chevron after it, so the dash marks a boundary that is already unmistakable. Only the separator is removed — no word changes.","value":"33 separators"},{"id":"items","on":true,"label":"Separate a link from its description","why":"33 list items open with a link and then explain it, all at the same weight — so the thing you can click is no easier to find than the sentence about it. The link becomes the item and the explanation sits under it.","value":"33 items"},{"id":"descap","on":true,"label":"Start a description with a capital","why":"1 description begins with a small letter, because it used to run on from the link after a dash. The dash is gone and the link now sits above in its own face, so each description opens a line of its own. One character changes and only ever the first.","value":"1 description"},{"id":"toc","on":true,"label":"Add a contents list (5 sections)","why":"Built from the section headings already on the page. Below three sections a list is not a route."},{"id":"eyebrow","on":true,"label":"Eyebrow: \"Essential Programs and Services (EPS) Funding\"","why":"Taken from the parent page, /funding/gpa/eps."}],"me